WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.251 --> 00:00:02.451
- It's funny, you know, you spend like,

00:00:02.451 --> 00:00:06.448
all of your 20's trying so so
so hard not to get pregnant,

00:00:06.448 --> 00:00:09.432
and then when you decide that it's time,

00:00:09.432 --> 00:00:11.688
that you wouldn't have any trouble,

00:00:11.688 --> 00:00:13.749
because it seems like it's such a threat

00:00:13.749 --> 00:00:15.321
when you're like, in your 20's.

00:00:15.321 --> 00:00:17.571
(laughter)

00:00:20.058 --> 00:00:21.557
- Do you remember how we met?

00:00:21.557 --> 00:00:23.437
- We met at a series of parties.

00:00:23.437 --> 00:00:24.368
I was like, you're not leaving

00:00:24.368 --> 00:00:25.568
until you give me your number.

00:00:25.568 --> 00:00:27.974
That was probably four years ago, now?

00:00:27.974 --> 00:00:29.503
- [Nathan] We started dating
in May, so, four years ago.

00:00:29.503 --> 00:00:30.412
- April.

00:00:30.412 --> 00:00:31.294
- Yeah.

00:00:31.294 --> 00:00:32.865
(laughter)

00:00:32.865 --> 00:00:35.588
- One day I saw a picture
of Nathan with a beard,

00:00:35.588 --> 00:00:36.686
holding a baby.

00:00:36.686 --> 00:00:38.966
And I was like, I think
maybe this is the guy

00:00:38.966 --> 00:00:40.956
that I need to have babies with.

00:00:40.956 --> 00:00:43.617
We've been living together for
about two and a half years.

00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:45.593
When I got pregnant the first time.

00:00:45.593 --> 00:00:47.668
- [Nathan] We told our family immediately,

00:00:47.668 --> 00:00:49.508
we really were like, oh, it's on,

00:00:49.508 --> 00:00:50.341
this is...

00:00:50.341 --> 00:00:51.905
- This is happening.
- What could go wrong?

00:00:51.905 --> 00:00:54.185
- We had an ultrasound
at about eight weeks,

00:00:54.185 --> 00:00:57.665
and the embryo didn't have a heartbeat.

00:00:57.665 --> 00:01:00.373
- They said, basically,
there's not a fetus there.

00:01:00.373 --> 00:01:01.834
- It was like a total shock,

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:03.694
the ultrasound lady was like,

00:01:03.694 --> 00:01:04.527
"Hmm..."

00:01:06.903 --> 00:01:08.730
"So, lemme go get the doctor."

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:10.753
- I mean, you know rationally
that what the doctors

00:01:10.753 --> 00:01:12.961
told you was true, but I
think part of you is still

00:01:12.961 --> 00:01:15.193
trying to figure out the
solution to the problem.

00:01:15.193 --> 00:01:18.044
- So I had a D&amp;C, which stands for

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:20.127
dissection and curettage.

00:01:21.095 --> 00:01:24.177
I didn't realize that I was
gonna be continuing to bleed

00:01:24.177 --> 00:01:25.546
for the next two weeks.

00:01:25.546 --> 00:01:28.548
Which was a constant reminder.

00:01:28.548 --> 00:01:32.276
I felt like a failure, like I wasn't sure,

00:01:32.276 --> 00:01:34.065
why this had to happen to me.

00:01:34.065 --> 00:01:35.847
I was so excited to have a baby,

00:01:35.847 --> 00:01:39.284
and it was like, where do we go from here?

00:01:39.284 --> 00:01:41.017
But, I did get pregnant again.

00:01:41.017 --> 00:01:41.850
- Uh huh.

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:43.887
- But I also had another miscarriage.

00:01:43.887 --> 00:01:45.185
And I talked to my doctor about it.

00:01:45.185 --> 00:01:47.105
She said, it's a really good sign,

00:01:47.105 --> 00:01:49.583
that it means that you
can get pregnant again.

00:01:49.583 --> 00:01:50.625
- And then, we did.

00:01:50.625 --> 00:01:51.764
- And then we did.

00:01:51.764 --> 00:01:53.247
- We did again, after that.

00:01:53.247 --> 00:01:54.607
- There was a third miscarriage.

00:01:54.607 --> 00:01:57.327
- With each one, two things happened.

00:01:57.327 --> 00:01:59.495
The shock of it isn't as extreme,

00:01:59.495 --> 00:02:01.167
'cause you've been through it.

00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:02.817
But you also start to wonder,

00:02:02.817 --> 00:02:05.145
is there something wrong
with our chemistry together?

00:02:05.145 --> 00:02:06.806
Is it maybe just isn't gonna happen?

00:02:06.806 --> 00:02:08.316
It was a hard time, it was a hard time

00:02:08.316 --> 00:02:11.767
for several weeks, months, afterwards.

00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:15.367
- All it really took was
one quick Google search,

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:17.876
and I found out that I wasn't alone.

00:02:17.876 --> 00:02:19.316
Before I was pregnant the first time,

00:02:19.316 --> 00:02:22.945
I didn't really know that many people

00:02:22.945 --> 00:02:24.417
who had had miscarriages.

00:02:24.417 --> 00:02:26.464
If you don't share with people,

00:02:26.464 --> 00:02:28.817
then you don't have a support system.

00:02:28.817 --> 00:02:30.607
We had decided to stop trying.

00:02:30.607 --> 00:02:32.316
- Yeah.
- After a while.

00:02:32.316 --> 00:02:35.196
- And then, two days after
that official choice...

00:02:35.196 --> 00:02:36.625
- We found out that I was pregnant.

00:02:36.625 --> 00:02:37.964
(laughter)

00:02:37.964 --> 00:02:40.697
- Today, I am 18 1/2 weeks pregnant.

00:02:40.697 --> 00:02:44.716
We were like, incredibly,
incredibly cautious.

00:02:44.716 --> 00:02:45.807
- And we told nobody.

00:02:45.807 --> 00:02:47.945
- I refused to believe that it was real,

00:02:47.945 --> 00:02:49.857
until I saw a heartbeat.

00:02:49.857 --> 00:02:50.955
- There was a lot of anxiety

00:02:50.955 --> 00:02:52.596
leading up to the first ultrasound.

00:02:52.596 --> 00:02:54.425
- Here we are at the doctor's office,

00:02:54.425 --> 00:02:56.543
about to have our NT ultrasound.

00:02:56.543 --> 00:03:01.516
And, I just hope that
everything's in the right place.

00:03:01.516 --> 00:03:03.016
We went in, and...

00:03:04.663 --> 00:03:06.516
- It was real.
- We had a heartbeat.

00:03:06.516 --> 00:03:08.607
The genetic counselor called me.

00:03:08.607 --> 00:03:10.145
- Right away, on the phonecall,

00:03:10.145 --> 00:03:12.297
she was like, "And, do
you want to know the sex?"

00:03:12.297 --> 00:03:15.380
Are we gonna find this out right now?

00:03:17.536 --> 00:03:19.092
- Oh, my goodness, wow!

00:03:19.092 --> 00:03:19.925
Are you ready?

00:03:19.925 --> 00:03:20.758
- No, no, yeah.

00:03:20.758 --> 00:03:21.641
- And she goes...

00:03:21.641 --> 00:03:24.636
- Okay, well it looks like
she has two x chromosomes.

00:03:24.636 --> 00:03:26.136
- She!
- Oh my god!

00:03:27.897 --> 00:03:29.457
- [Nathan] It was
awesome when we found out

00:03:29.457 --> 00:03:31.636
that we are having a baby girl.

00:03:31.636 --> 00:03:32.777
- We're having a girl.

00:03:32.777 --> 00:03:33.765
(laughter)

00:03:33.765 --> 00:03:37.207
- The second ultrasound, we did
another one at 12 weeks ish.

00:03:37.207 --> 00:03:39.156
- [Nathan] Yeah, the ultrasound
technician was awesome,

00:03:39.156 --> 00:03:42.247
she was like, look there's her
feet, look there's the hands,

00:03:42.247 --> 00:03:43.097
there's the face!

00:03:43.097 --> 00:03:45.708
And like, printed out
numerous photos for us,

00:03:45.708 --> 00:03:47.276
and it was way more fun.

00:03:47.276 --> 00:03:48.695
- [Angela] Way more fun.

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:49.793
- [Nathan] Oh my goodness.

00:03:49.793 --> 00:03:50.996
- [Angela] Is that her foot, right there?

00:03:50.996 --> 00:03:52.537
- [Nathan] There's like, tons of action.

00:03:52.537 --> 00:03:55.487
- And that's when we decided
that it was gonna be okay

00:03:55.487 --> 00:03:56.617
to tell our families.

00:03:56.617 --> 00:03:57.450
- Yeah.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:00.148
- [Angela] Nathan cut out a
cute little sign that said like,

00:04:00.148 --> 00:04:01.428
it's a girl!

00:04:01.428 --> 00:04:03.577
- [Nathan] And then we started
this Skype with a monitor

00:04:03.577 --> 00:04:06.114
bent down towards us, so
they couldn't see the wall.

00:04:06.114 --> 00:04:08.076
And so we kinda hunched down.

00:04:08.076 --> 00:04:10.548
- With our faces cut off right here.

00:04:10.548 --> 00:04:12.257
- And then at a certain
point, we tried to get

00:04:12.257 --> 00:04:15.948
them to say, "Hey, I can't
really see you that well."

00:04:15.948 --> 00:04:18.802
- [Angela] Can you see
us okay, or should we...?

00:04:18.802 --> 00:04:21.884
- Well, we can see half of Nathan's head.

00:04:21.884 --> 00:04:26.051
- Nathan, adjust your, we're
cut off around your eyes.

00:04:27.821 --> 00:04:29.833
- The key moment, tilted the screen back,

00:04:29.833 --> 00:04:31.623
and then we just kept talking.

00:04:31.623 --> 00:04:32.790
- There ya go.

00:04:33.665 --> 00:04:36.295
- It's a girl, what does that mean?

00:04:36.295 --> 00:04:37.785
- Tilt the screen a little.

00:04:37.785 --> 00:04:40.092
- Yeah, there you go, that's good.

00:04:40.092 --> 00:04:41.865
Oh, hey, wow!

00:04:41.865 --> 00:04:46.133
- We got to see them be like. (sputters)

00:04:46.133 --> 00:04:47.794
- Hey, what's goin' on!

00:04:47.794 --> 00:04:49.405
(laughter)

00:04:49.405 --> 00:04:50.488
- Oh my gosh!

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:54.673
(laughter)

00:04:54.673 --> 00:04:55.673
- Oh my god!

00:04:58.753 --> 00:05:00.681
- [Nathan] You're a grandpa, or will be.

00:05:00.681 --> 00:05:03.214
- [Angela] Almost, I mean.

00:05:03.214 --> 00:05:04.464
- [Nathan] Aww.

00:05:05.803 --> 00:05:06.793
- It was very fun.

00:05:06.793 --> 00:05:08.537
- It was super cute.

00:05:08.537 --> 00:05:13.017
I learned a lot during
my first pregnancies.

00:05:13.017 --> 00:05:15.497
I guess I just wanna say,
like, for other women

00:05:15.497 --> 00:05:17.907
and other couples who
are going through this,

00:05:17.907 --> 00:05:18.995
you are not alone.

00:05:18.995 --> 00:05:21.055
So, don't be afraid to reach out,

00:05:21.055 --> 00:05:23.135
don't be afraid to talk to your families

00:05:23.135 --> 00:05:24.563
and your friends about it.

00:05:24.563 --> 00:05:26.194
- Stay hopeful, keep your plans intact,

00:05:26.194 --> 00:05:28.467
just keep working towards
the result that you need.

00:05:28.467 --> 00:05:31.217
- Healthy pregnancies after a miscarriage

00:05:31.217 --> 00:05:33.217
are a total possibility.

